WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:03.830 align:start position:0%
 
it is  finally here  after a long wait the 32nd olympic games  are actually happening this summer  but tokyo 2020 will be unlike any games  we've seen before  here's why  tokyo 2020 was postponed and rescheduled  because of the covet 19 pandemic  the postponement has cost an estimated  2.5  billion pounds  the olympic games have never been  postponed or cancelled for anything  apart from war with the 1916  1940 and 1944 games  all being called off because of the  first and second world wars  obviously the biggest changes are all to  do with covet 19.  no spectators will be allowed to watch  the events in the tokyo stadiums  following a surge in cases of the delta  variant  japan has declared a coronavirus state  of emergency for the capital  that will run throughout the event that  means public viewings of the games  have been cancelled restaurants and bars  will even be asked to stop  serving alcohol  [Music]  in short a lot  international competitors will be tested  before departure  and as they arrive in the country while  in japan  they need to stay in their bubbles and  not mix with locals  they will then be regularly tested for  kobit  [Music]  the iconic olympic torch relay has  already been drastically affected  by the coveted walls  it's been diverted from busy areas with  multiple athletes pulling out  over fears about drawing crowds that  could help spread the pandemic  [Music]  putting the pandemic to one side for a  moment there are some exciting changes  coming to  tokyo 2020 we have five new sports  surfing skateboarding baseball softball  karate and sports climbing the games  will also see  skateboarder sky brown become britain's  youngest summer olympian  she'll be 13 years and 11 days old  when she competes in tokyo it means  the world to me i mean i it's gonna be  really fun  and i'm excited to represent tinkerine  [Applause]  [Music]  team gb is sending its largest team ever  for an overseas olympics  for the first time in history there are  more female  the male athletes competing  it will be a time where there will be  more females on the tv at any one time  than you'll ever see  and i just think that is such um a  brilliant thing for the younger  generation coming through  tokyo 2020 will also see the first  transgender athlete competing  laurel hubbard was selected for new  zealand's weightlifting team  after meeting all the requirements set  out by the ioc  for trans athletes  tokyo 2020 has become a controversial  subject across the country  according to the nikkei newspaper 63  of the japanese public are opposed to  holding the games  critics say bringing an estimated 90 000  athletes  officials journalists and other workers  into japan  isn't the best idea in a pandemic  japan has handled the coronavirus better  than most  but some fear this could be unravelled  by hosting the games  but all the complaints and protests have  not changed the organizers minds  with one senior olympic official saying  the only thing that will stop these  games  is armageddon

